{"skill":{"slug":"discord-chat","displayName":"Discord Chat"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769502876749,"changelog":"Initial release: Send messages, reply, search history, and manage Discord channels","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3216,"sha256":"d6b43b86cfb65787aec734fbc49760c6189b312186080835fb9d7fbbdcdf9c2b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/CHANNELS.md","size":4451,"sha256":"56fe09d2eef7085c2f5b741fd6b5fd0270cb1338ea58adee7b4c5d01cfed15e4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/CONFIG.md","size":4306,"sha256":"c910999caedeae2548a0a91e0ef08e586ee85355075d2a915737ecf946d7df83","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/SEARCH.md","size":2579,"sha256":"d46aea06a312be6253ec04462b4e4a15db0bb3e41da45fcd7025fcf0647461e6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2435,"sha256":"a058c46434e63ae903140563cf88c73c7dd47a01a4e7b1470f534aaac1b0a220","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021919330,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c277e9dd7ac09bdfa0c018032921119a6de1d14c7def2a995061a2a2c78040ab","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c277e9dd7ac09bdfa0c018032921119a6de1d14c7def2a995061a2a2c78040ab","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: discord-chat\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides comprehensive documentation for interacting with Discord via a `message` tool, covering standard operations like sending messages, managing channels, and searching. All instructions are clearly defined Discord API operations. The `CONFIG.md` file explicitly recommends strong security practices for bot configuration, such as using environment variables for tokens and limiting permissions. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the agent to perform actions beyond the stated purpose of Discord interaction.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160112784},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789021919330},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Discord skill is not clearly malicious, but it exposes server-management and deletion actions that go beyond its chat-focused description and need careful review before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Messaging permissions are proportionate for a Discord chat skill, but documented channel/category administration and multi-guild operation are broader than the stated chat/search purpose and can affect real Discord servers.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No executable installer or embedded code was present; setup is documentation-only, but it instructs users to configure bot tokens, webhooks, gateway config, and even allows webhook secrets in query parameters.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill gives direct commands for destructive Discord operations using opaque IDs, with only limited warnings and no mandatory confirmation, target preview, or clear separation between chat actions and administrative actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"There is no host persistence, background worker, or privilege escalation, but the documented Discord actions can create persistent external changes such as edited channels, pins, deleted messages, and deleted channels/categories.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The manifest describes sending, replying to, searching, checking activity, and interacting with Discord channels, but the artifacts also document message edit/delete plus channel/category create, edit, move, delete, permissions, pins, and thread operations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend the agent to perform live Discord operations and can tightly limit the bot's permissions. Use least-privilege Discord roles, avoid granting channel/category management unless needed, do not put webhook secrets in URLs, and require explicit confirmation before any edit, delete, move, or channel/category action.","findings":"[SDI-4] unexpected: Accepted in substance: CHANNELS.md documents channel creation, editing, moving, and deletion, which is materially broader than the chat/search framing.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Accepted in part: the artifacts disclose broader Discord read/write/admin actions than the manifest highlights; this is under-scoped rather than evidence of hidden code or exfiltration.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted in part: channel and category lifecycle operations can affect server integrity and availability, but the artifact does not show Discord permission bypass or host compromise.\n[P1] expected: Downgraded: 'Enable Developer Mode' is Discord setup guidance for copying IDs, not an instruction to override the agent's safety rules.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Accepted: the invocation text is broad enough to route generic Discord requests into a skill that also documents destructive and administrative operations.\n[SQP-2] expected: Accepted as an operational safety concern: deleting messages may fit Discord management, but the skill does not require explicit confirmation or target verification.\n[T09] expected: Accepted as a configuration safety issue: the webhook setup allows secrets in query parameters, which is unnecessary and weaker than header or signature-based verification.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021919330}}}}}